{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788130021,"nonce":"X2t3DT+lO5zBXoWUntgADGcNRsg=","message":"CLOSING EVIDENCE — branch `spec/2.6-observer-remediation`, 8 commits, DLL last.\n\nBench `_RimWorld-Agent` only, four boots, `--quicktest` 250x250 maps. All figures\nbelow are from the FINAL boot against the COMMITTED artifact (7e83f9b,\nInformationalVersion 1.0.0+10ff739..., pdb path\n`/home/dorian/projects/rimworld/autorimmer/Source/AutoRimmer/obj/Release/AutoRimmer.pdb`,\nAssemblyConfiguration Release, Debug blob absent) unless a line says otherwise.\n\nBLOCKER 1 — find-rect. The acceptance line asks for the 2.3 closing-evidence\ncase to return [112,130]. It does, on two different map seeds:\n\n    find-rect {w:5,h:7,near:[114,133],max:3}\n    [{'at': [112,130], 'center': [114,133], 'dist': 0},\n     {'at': [112,129], 'center': [114,132], 'dist': 1},\n     {'at': [112,131], 'center': [114,134], 'dist': 1}]\n\n[112,130] is Chebyshev ring 3 from `near` in ORIGIN space, which is why 2.3's\norigin-space walk never reached it. On the first boot I also confirmed the rect\nwith ORIGIN at `near` is itself buildable and sits at dist 3.6 — that is\nprecisely the candidate 2.3 returned first.\n\nTermination is proven, and says so when it is not:\n\n    find-rect {w:12,h:12,near:\u003ccolony\u003e,require:[\"buildable\",\"roofed\"],max:5}\n    candidates []  examined 6001  searched_radius 39  capped True\n    rejected {'unroofed': 5317, 'edifice-in-way': 437, 'fogged': 246}\n\nBLOCKER 2 — alerts. 15 injected with the Critical LAST (journal `alert_on`\narrival order: seq 26 Medium, seq 27 Critical — position 15 of 15):\n\n    total 15  shown 12  more 3  more_by_priority {'Medium': 3}\n    shown[0]: Alert_AutoRimmerFixtureCritical / Critical\n\nUnder 2.1's `live[0..11]` the Critical at index 14 was the one cut.\n\nBLOCKER 3 — colonist cap, on a 20-colonist colony, same digest both ways:\n\n    CAPPED (default 10)  digest 1639 B   colonists section  981 B  more 10\n    UNCAPPED (cap 200)   digest 2560 B   colonists section 1902 B  more 0\n\nThe uncapped figure is what 2.1 shipped. Its Caveat 1 extrapolated ~2.1KB; the\nmeasurement is 1902 B for the section alone and 2560 B for the digest, i.e. the\ncaveat was right that it breached the budget and wrong that it was unmeasured.\n\nBLOCKER 4 — map-view radius. `{radius:30}` -\u003e ok, 61x61, 61 rows.\n`{radius:31}` -\u003e bad-args \"radius must be 1..30\".\n\nSHOULD-FIX 5 — power, three states, each agreeing with the def-derived\nexpectation the fixture returns alongside:\n\n    unfuelled generator + battery + 2 lamps (expect gen 0, draw 60)\n      gen_w 0     draw_w 60   gain_w -60  stored_wd 299  battery_days 4.99\n    + a second, fuelled grid          (expect gen 1000, draw 60)\n      gen_w 1000  draw_w 120  gain_w 880  stored_wd 605  battery_days null\n                                          nets 2  nets_with_generator 2\n    battery-only grid, isolated       (the rider)\n      gen_w 0     draw_w 0    stored_wd 200  batteries 1\n                                          nets 1  nets_with_generator 0\n\nbattery_days 4.99 = 299 Wd / 60 W. The rider reads exactly as predicted: the\ngame's own `hasPowerSource` calls a bare battery a source, `nets_with_generator`\ndoes not.\n\nREMOVAL TAXONOMY — all four values observed on real map furniture, with the\ngame's own string where the game has one. From the first boot, one `find-rect`\ncall at the edge of a fogged pocket:\n\n    {'why':'fogged',          'def':None,  'removal':'none',        'reason':'unexplored', 'count':129}\n    {'why':'edifice-in-way',  'def':'Limestone',              'removal':'mine',        'reason':None, 'count':52}\n    {'why':'edifice-in-way',  'def':'Wall',                   'removal':'deconstruct',  'reason':None, 'count':29}\n    {'why':'edifice-in-way',  'def':'AncientWarwalkerTorso',  'removal':'attack',\n     'reason':'Remove this by attacking it.', 'count':4}\n    {'why':'edifice-in-way',  'def':'MineableComponentsIndustrial', 'removal':'mine', 'count':2}\n\nFOG — `map-view` legend carries `\"?\": \"unexplored (fogged)\"` with 65-165 fogged\ncells shaped correctly in the crop; `find-rect` near a fogged pocket puts its\nfirst candidate 6.4 cells away in explored ground and tallies `fogged: 46`;\n`room-at` on a fogged cell returns `{room:null, fogged:true, removal:\"none\",\nreason:\"unexplored\"}`; `reachable` into fog reports `to_fogged:true` and refuses\nto name what is under it.\n\nRESERVED BAND — legend from a live 61x61 crop:\n`\"@\": \"colonist (Kees,Steroid,Aes)\"`, `\"^\": \"tame animal (Tallyho)\"`,\n`\"g\": \"granite chunk\"`, `\"w\": \"wood\"`. Under 2.3 `g` and `w` were guest and wild\nanimal and the legend merged the two meanings into one string.\n\nNITS — `nearest {def:\"MinifiedThing\"}` returns ok with no red error;\n`map-view {rect:[-60,-60,10,10]}` is bad-args \"lies entirely outside the 250x250\nmap\" while `[-3,-3,8,8]` still clips to `origin [0,0] 5x5 clipped:true`;\n`threats.kinds` sorts by count; `since`/`since_seq` read as long.\n\nZERO RED ERRORS held on every boot: journal `red_error` count 0, LogRelay\n0 errors / 9 warnings — the identical FINDINGS section 5 baseline set (SteamAPI\nx1, Guests/Socio-Butterfly x2, StaticConstructorOnStartup x6). Build: 0 warnings,\n0 errors. Two builds at the same HEAD are byte-identical (cmp -l: 0).\n\nWHAT I DID NOT DEMONSTRATE\n- **The in-game power tab.** The acceptance line says \"verified against the\n  in-game power tab\". I did not read the game's UI: that needs a human at the\n  screen to select a conduit, and this bench runs parked and unattended. What I\n  substituted is two independent routes agreeing — the def XML\n  (`WoodFiredGenerator` basePowerConsumption -1000, `StandingLamp` 30) and the\n  live `PowerNet.powerComps` walk. `gain_w` is also the same quantity\n  `CompPower`'s inspect string prints (`CurrentEnergyGainRate() /\n  WattsToWattDaysPerTick`). Dorian can confirm in one glance if he wants it\n  closed properly.\n- **Should-fix 7, designations over things.** No shipped verb creates a\n  designation, 3.2 owns `designate`, and a 60x60 sweep of the map found none to\n  render. I declined to add a fifth fixture step for it because that step would\n  be 3.2's verb in all but name. The change is a block move in\n  `CropRenderer.Cell` and is reviewable in the diff, but it is untested in-game.\n- **The `job_error` path.** No JobDriver on the bench threw during the run, so\n  the new surfacing is code-reviewed only.\n- **Long-lived `since`.** The `Long` getter fixes a narrowing that only bites\n  past 2^31; no session reaches that, so it is reasoned, not exercised.\n- **Save/load of any of this.** Nothing here adds persisted state, and I did not\n  re-run 2.3's landmark round-trip.\n\nFLAGGED\n- 2.3's closing-comment glyph table is now stale (guest/tame/wild moved off\n  g/d/w). The catalog.py cross-check that RUNLOG session 2 parked as a\n  before-3.2/3.3 item must be done against the new band.\n- The `reachable` fog leak was mine, introduced in this spec and caught by its\n  own acceptance run rather than by review. It is the argument for running one.","files":null}]}